# Adds a Howdy IR face-auth path to the Omarchy lock plugin, alongside the
# built-in password and fingerprint PAM flows. When the lock comes up after
# 20 s without input (idle timeout) or on resume, the scan starts at once.
# When locked while active (Super+Ctrl+L), it waits for a key or trackpad
# press, so locking at the desk does not unlock straight away.
#
# It also makes the lock screen look like Omarchy's boot unlock screen instead
# of the blurred wallpaper, and follow whichever style you pick in Omarchy's
# menu under Style > Unlock (Default or any theme's): the same logo, padlock,
# background and text colour, re-read on every lock. Pixel-art logos are drawn
# at exactly 2x with smoothing off, so they stay sharp on HiDPI screens.
#
# Made against Omarchy 4.0.4's lock plugin (checksums in lock/UPSTREAM_SHA256).
# Apply to a clone, never to /usr/share/omarchy:
#
#   omarchy plugin clone omarchy.lock          # creates ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/$USER.lock
#   cd ~/.config/omarchy/plugins/$USER.lock && patch -p1 < face-lock.patch
#   omarchy restart shell
#
